<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The Fundamental Problems=
:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No Standard</strong>: M=
ultiple competing systems (AMD, CommonJS, UMD, globals)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Runtime Dependency Reso=
lution</strong>: Modules loaded v=C3=A0 resolved at runtime</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No Static Analysis</str=
ong>: Build tools couldn't analyze dependencies</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Global Namespace Pollut=
ion</strong>: Risk of naming conflicts</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Manual Dependency Manag=
ement</strong>: Developers manually track dependencies</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No Tree Shaking</strong=
>: Impossible to remove unused code</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Load Order Dependencies=
</strong>: Script tag order mattered</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=92=AD <strong>Personal Ho=
rror Story</strong>: "T=E1=BA=A1i Webflow, ch=C3=BAng t=C3=B4i had a bug wh=
ere modal component wouldn't work on production but worked fine locally. Af=
ter 6 hours debugging, discovered that script concatenation order was diffe=
rent trong build process, causing utils.js to load after components.js. Wit=
h ES6 modules, this class of bugs completely disappeared."</p>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=94=AC B=E1=BA=
